From 8fa57c367de2b0da8535d5761e349c9576b4ce4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:08:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Offer a half and full snap for the tab sheet, with a
 draggable handle.

Opening the sheet now settles at a half-height stop so the page stays
visible above it. A scrim sits over that page and closes the sheet when
tapped. Dragging the handle moves the sheet with the finger; when the
list is at the top, a downward over-pull does the same. On release the
sheet snaps by position and fling velocity: up to full, down to half,
or down from half to close. Full leaves a small gap below the status
bar, as in the mockup.

The side drawer is unchanged. The same list, drag-reorder and
swipe-to-close are used in both styles. Animation uses a decelerate
curve. The snap decision is in BareTabSheetSnap so it can be tested
without the view.

Tested on the Android emulator (Pixel 10 Pro profile).
